    "<entry>",
    "<id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/41fc8c2c0029acba7ec7c3ef4eadf87868b74895</id>",
    "<link type=\"text/html\" rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://github.com/YukonWRB/AquaCache/commit/41fc8c2c0029acba7ec7c3ef4eadf87868b74895\"/>",
    "<title>",
    "Replace apply_from cutoff with protection of readings",
    "</title>",
    "<updated>2026-11-03T19:04:43Z</updated>",
    "<media:thumbnail height=\"30\" width=\"30\" url=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132517733?s=30&amp;v=4\"/>",
    "<author>",
    "<name>EmmaGRiley</name>",
    "<uri>https://github.com/EmmaGRiley</uri>",
    "</author>",
    "<content type=\"html\">",
    "&lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Replace apply_from cutoff with protection of readings",
    "gradeContinuous() now leaves readings covered by a protected range of any managed code alone, instead of only blocking new ranges of the same type. Protection survives a re-sync as well as a regrade, which apply_from did not, so the apply_from column is removed from timeseries_qc_rules.&lt;/pre&gt;",
    "</content>",
    "</entry>",
    "<entry>",
    "<id>tag:github.com,2008:Grit::Commit/2d05757014c2d9a8088827ae5a2d36a83815e027</id>",
    "<link type=\"text/html\" rel=\"alternate\" href=\"https://github.com/YukonWRB/AquaCache/commit/2d05757014c2d9a8088827ae5a2d36a83815e027\"/>",
    "<title>",
    "Add post-import QC grading for continuous timeseries",
    "</title>",
    "<updated>2026-11-02T22:14:57Z</updated>",
    "<media:thumbnail height=\"30\" width=\"30\" url=\"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/132517733?s=30&amp;v=4\"/>",
    "<author>",
    "<name>EmmaGRiley</name>",
    "<uri>https://github.com/EmmaGRiley</uri>",
    "</author>",
    "<content type=\"html\">",
    "&lt;pre style=&#39;white-space:pre-wrap;width:81ex&#39;&gt;Add post-import QC grading for continuous timeseries",
    "Adds gradeContinuous(), which applies QC rules assigned per timeseries and writes results to continuous.qualifiers. It runs after getNewContinuous() and synchronize_continuous() under a SAVEPOINT, so a grading failure leaves the import committed. The patch (patch_XX_qc_rules.R, numbered at merge) adds public.qc_rule_capabilities and continuous.timeseries_qc_rules, mirroring patch 56, seeds four rules (qc_rain_cold, qc_stuck_sensor, qc_dir_calm, qc_snowmelt_tips) and adds the qualifier types CT, SSM and PSM. Includes unit tests.&lt;/pre&gt;",
    "</content>",
    "</entry>",
